{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred","id":163531,"title":"If Shapechangers were Chosen instead of Bred","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-09T06:52:22-07:00","id":163531,"title":"If Shapechangers were Chosen instead of Bred","content":"So I had this idea regarding the changing breeds and werewolves. It sort of came to me after reading notes from the developers of the Idigam Chronicles. What if each shifter, rather than being tied to an ancient bloodline, were instead chosen by agents of the Incarna? If they passed a trial of sorts, they become full-fledged theiromorphs. Each Incarna's trial is different, and some might even be fatal. Other times they seem almost random in their choosing of new candidates. Hell, perhaps some only choose those related to past chosen, giving reason to valuing bloodline heritage like with the Ivory Claws. Where Luna comes in is that she can add an additional blessing to Father Wolf's children, but only if they swear to her Oath. Otherwise the new Uratha is without her patronage.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T07:22:42-07:00","id":163561,"title":"","content":"I believe that's what they're changing to, with Idigam Chronicles.<br /> And, honestly, I've always run it that way. I think Blood of the Wolf says otherwise, but I never got it, so just going from the core I always played with them sort of like Exalted, though not quite to the level you suggest. Many times you have a bloodline, but occasionally you're just chosen at random. Sometimes wolf blood families just...thin out until they're all mortal.<br /> <br /> Though if you wanted to get really weird about it, considering werewolves have existed since before the dawn of civilization, it's possible everyone is, however distantly, descended from a werewolf, making 'random' Changes more like severely distant lineage-based changes. There's some options in the Chronicler's guide about how to make it bite-transmitted I believe, and other options.<br /> <br /> The problem with having this involved with other shapechangers is that most aren't involved with Incarna. There's the Baal-hadad, chosen of Helios, but the others have different origin stories that involve beings less powerful than the Incarna, who, outside of Luna, we don't get much in-depth writing on.<br /> <br /> Also, a Forsaken who abandons or refuses Luna is a Pure. Or occasionally a Bale Hound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-09-2014, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T07:55:09-07:00","id":163590,"title":"","content":"I know, that's what I meant, that or a Ghost Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:30:00-07:00","id":163673,"title":"","content":"It's how I've always handled becoming a werewolf. Wolf blood is in no way a necessary component. If the insane moon decides you should be a werewolf, then you will be.<br /> <br /> I don't like the idea of a trial so much, though - I prefer leaving things up to the moon, quite simply. Being a werewolf isn't anything a sane person wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:55:54-07:00","id":163713,"title":"","content":"Early on, I tried working around the Father Wolf/Mother Moon myths, I had each of the Tribal Totems picking their &quot;chosen ones&quot; and grabbed them under whatever phase of the moon they liked them to have. Luna still got her input, but the Totems were the ones trying to swell their ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:58:22-07:00","id":163716,"title":"","content":"Thing is, Ghost Wolves are part of the Forsaken. They're blessed by Luna like everyone else, they just refuse to pick another totem by joining one of the major tribes.<br /> <br /> Starting out unchosen would make everyone start off as a Pure, then choose to be Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T16:14:12-07:00","id":164179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=163713#post163713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early on, I tried working around the Father Wolf/Mother Moon myths, I had each of the Tribal Totems picking their &quot;chosen ones&quot; and grabbed them under whatever phase of the moon they liked them to have. Luna still got her input, but the Totems were the ones trying to swell their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing like the act of Impressment to swell one's ranks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T06:25:02-07:00","id":168845,"title":"","content":"I started writing a werewolf story- unrelated to anything World of Darkness- where becoming a wolf was more complicated. Not only did you have to be born to a line of werewolves, but you had to be receive the <i>bite </i>(suffer a near death wound from another full fledged werewolf) to actually change, and thus become a werewolf. Not everyone who was born a werewolf could become a werewolf, and it was difficult to tell (for sure) who would become a wolf and who would not. Also, surviving the attack wasn't something a mere human was likely to do without major control on the attacker's part, something the monster wasn't known for.<br /> <br /> The real pain came from the later generations. Children and grand-children of the wolves were well tracked, but if no none of your great grandfather's siblings became the a wolf, no one really paid attention to you. Add a few more generations, with the various wolf family weak bloods intermingling, staying just strong enough to exist but not enough to make any child a wolf. And then, when the child has that prefect amount of weak blood to push him over the threshold pass being human, but not enough to become a wolf, you get a bastard. Should they survive the bite, they find themselves a little stronger, faster, and more perceptive. And when they shift, their get a tiny bite stronger, a tiny bit faster, their bones grow an inch or so, and so on. Their grow fangs (short one) but their jaw doesn't expand to make them useful (you get a mouthful of sharp teeth; you can't open it further, and you certainly can't close it).<br /> <br /> The whole story was an attempt to make a 'half-breed' story where the main character doesn't get the best of both worlds, and instead gets the worst. Character one began with the hero suffering from the common cold and <a href=\"http://www.petmd.com/dog/conditions/respiratory/c_dg_canine_influenza\" target=\"_blank\">dog flu</a> at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3097-gator-the-unread","name":"Gator the Unread","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:18:24-07:00","id":199451,"title":"","content":"Some one liked my post! Awesome!<br /> <br /> This idea was spawned from a discussion about half-breeds. Almost all the time when you see a half-breed in fiction, is has the best of both worlds. A half-vampire would have all the vampire benefits (strength, speed, etc) and none of the weaknesses (walk around in daylight, able to eat juicy hamburgers, etc). All animal hybrids have all the benefits of being an animal (super senses, speed, etc) but none of the weaknesses (urge to pee on things, fleas, etc.). These, to me, weren't heroic characters, but super heroes without capes. Also very boring; there isn't any struggle is you are so much better than both of your halves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3097-gator-the-unread","name":"Gator the Unread","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:56:15-07:00","id":199477,"title":"","content":"Keep 'em coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T01:59:53-07:00","id":199815,"title":"","content":"Guess I'm the only one around who likes the idea of lineage better than being chosen. For me family is a great part and thus the aspect of family and lineage adds greatly to the game as it makes the characters operate in a context and have deeper and more complex, for me, relationships with other Uratha than just being random strangers who happens to have something in common. That's what makes the game different from Vampire and Mage and also makes the connection to Mother Luna different from her just, essentially, being a wannabe-Watchtower instead of a this mad ancestor-goddess.<br /> <br /> But I realize that some other people thinks differently and they are free to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T05:57:12-07:00","id":199917,"title":"","content":"Well, what if wolf-blooded weren't actually lupine by nature? What if every human on the planet was imbued with a piece of Pangaea? But certain mindsets, personalities, and places of origin amplified this shard to make it more prominent? Most people would have a potency that's in the .0 digits, but through breeding, proximity to loci, and connection to spiritual events, they're capable of becoming a shifter, and not necessarily a werewolf.<br /> <br /> No wolf-blooded, Spirit-blooded! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T15:35:15-07:00","id":200443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred#post163531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I had this idea regarding the changing breeds and werewolves. It sort of came to me after reading notes from the developers of the Idigam Chronicles. What if each shifter, rather than being tied to an ancient bloodline, were instead chosen by agents of the Incarna? If they passed a trial of sorts, they become full-fledged theiromorphs. Each Incarna's trial is different, and some might even be fatal. Other times they seem almost random in their choosing of new candidates. Hell, perhaps some only choose those related to past chosen, giving reason to valuing bloodline heritage like with the Ivory Claws. Where Luna comes in is that she can add an additional blessing to Father Wolf's children, but only if they swear to her Oath. Otherwise the new Uratha is without her patronage.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of set up is similar to another game I played called Shadowbane. In that game, Lycanthropy was not a disease one contracted, but a talent that one could learn with enough spiritual training and dedication. It had Rats, Wolves, and Bears as playable Lycanthropes, often involving some manner of quest to become recognized as worthy. They even had an origin story stating that the first Lycanthrope was visited by <b>animal spirits</b> who gave him the power to assume their forms.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also like the idea of being able to choose to become a Lycanthrope as opposed to it being forced upon you. I quite disapprove of the new generation of the myth saying you have to be born as one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-17-2014, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T15:36:13-07:00","id":200444,"title":"","content":"I've always run along the idea that werewolves have bred with humans for so long that practically anyone can change, but they're more likely to do so the closer they are to a werewolf ancestor in their family tree. The exact conditions that dictate turning are left purposefully ambiguous and imply that Luna has some sort of say in the matter, which explains why all werewolves are Forsaken when they turn barring ritual intervention. If nothing else it's rather forward that there's no way to know for certain if someone will change...except for the Lodge of the Hazzan, but they're weird and only predict if the child will change not under what conditions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:13:30-07:00","id":203508,"title":"","content":"I don't mind lineages, in fact I use them in my games. Wolf-Blooded families that are associated with a tribe that the members who become Forsaken tend to join.<br /> <br /> What I hate is &quot;born this way&quot; werewolves. It's too much Apocalypse for me, and one of the (many) changes from WtA that I enjoyed and made me like Forsaken that much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T04:55:02-07:00","id":204872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=203508#post203508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind lineages, in fact I use them in my games. Wolf-Blooded families that are associated with a tribe that the members who become Forsaken tend to join.<br /> <br /> What I hate is &quot;born this way&quot; werewolves. It's too much Apocalypse for me, and one of the (many) changes from WtA that I enjoyed and made me like Forsaken that much more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woh! Amaterasu! Origin of all that is good, and mother to us all! Such an honor! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T20:33:01-07:00","id":206749,"title":"","content":"The only Werewolves in W:tF that have any real ties to breeding are the Ivory Claws, every other tribe cares little about breeding, so if you make werewolves chosen instead of bred, it would only cause problem with one Pure tribe, which you could make to be that they believe that they can get being a werewolf to breed true, instead of just people being chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T02:34:53-07:00","id":208051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=206749#post206749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only Werewolves in W:tF that have any real ties to breeding are the Ivory Claws, every other tribe cares little about breeding, so if you make werewolves chosen instead of bred, it would only cause problem with one Pure tribe, which you could make to be that they believe that they can get being a werewolf to breed true, instead of just people being chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>This flies in the face of &quot;Cleave to the Human&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:15:55-07:00","id":208981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=208051#post208051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This flies in the face of &quot;Cleave to the Human&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If werewolves are chosen instead of bred, then cleave to the human may not be necessary to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T01:52:20-07:00","id":209940,"title":"","content":"Cleave to the human won't matter after idigam anyway. I'm greatly curious to see the new laws of the moon, considering unihar are largely gone. And I prefer bred/turned. If there's a way to turn a wolf blooded into a werewolf id be ok with that. Chosen gives them this important feel that's big in apocalypse, but I wouldn't like in forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T15:07:06-07:00","id":210601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kurasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=208981#post208981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If werewolves are chosen instead of bred, then cleave to the human may not be necessary to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Let's forget the sexual subtext. What would 'cleaving to the human' mean then? I'll spell it out for you: Don't forget from where you come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T14:58:56-07:00","id":217589,"title":"","content":"I've always played my Uratha having been chosen for two reasons in particular.<br /> <br /> 1) If there are specific genetic markers in the human body that can be pointed to in the World of Darkness as &quot;the werewolf gene,&quot; then that creates a whole mess of problems I have to explain away as to why hunter agencies don't snuff out wolf-blooded with impunity after a little routine bloodwork. I'll add the caveat that this one only matters if you're running a game with organized human hunters though.<br /> <br /> 2) Given the statistical likelihood that everyone shares a common ancestor as far back as <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BhtgINeaJWg\" target=\"_blank\">300 BC</a> then it becomes a lot harder to find someone who didn't get a little contribution from a Pre-Sumerian flirtation with Father Wolf's children, much less from time immemorial before that. Naturally, the gene might not carry forward, but it still makes any one person you pick out on the street a very likely carrier.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I simply find the moment more evocative when a finger from on high points at you and says &quot;You. You will bear this yoke. You will wear the night and moon as your cloak and shackles. You will be Uratha.&quot; Werewolves in the World of Darkness are driven creatures of undeniable instinct, so making the Change an epiphany just fits for me. Whenever I get to play through a prologue with players, the moment is painted in fractured visions of Luna and his purpose for her child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T15:47:36-07:00","id":217618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tilting Clock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=217589#post217589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) If there are specific genetic markers in the human body that can be pointed to in the World of Darkness as &quot;the werewolf gene,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me stop you right here: there isn't. It's implied to be a spiritual lineage, which is why you hear more about werewolf efforts to trace family trees to notable ancestors than Uratha geneticists.<br /> <br /> I've read literally the entire corpus of published Werewolf books in the last year and not once do I recall mention of any sort of attempts to leverage sperm banks or IVF or other subsections of fertility science. Given the way spirits in general work, it's probably not an accident.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood of the Wolf p102, &quot;Raised by Wolves&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As stated in Werewolf: The Forsaken, a person related to a werewolf might be wolf-blooded. It\u2019s not as simple as tracing a blood connection to one of the Uratha, though. A distant cousin of a werewolf might find that the spiritual line of the wolf runs strong in her veins, while the son of another might be meek and fearful all his life. The \u201cblessing\u201d of Urfarah is fickle, and is more a matter of spirit than genetics.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> then that creates a whole mess of problems I have to explain away as to why hunter agencies don't snuff out wolf-blooded with impunity after a little routine bloodwork. </div> </div> </div>Because a) the &quot;kill their families, that'll solve things!&quot; hunters are fuckawful people who rightly tend to get lumped in with the rest of the serial murderers in the World of Darkness, 2) many werewolves fake their deaths after the First Change and a significant number of them live off the grid besides, and \u0393) bits of a werewolf that come off revert to human form and the human form is one of the two that actively interfere with attempts to discern its owner as anything supernatural and there are maybe half a million werewolves in the <i>world</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Given the statistical likelihood that everyone shares a common ancestor as far back as <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BhtgINeaJWg\" target=\"_blank\">300 BC</a> then it becomes a lot harder to find someone who didn't get a little contribution from a Pre-Sumerian flirtation with Father Wolf's children, much less from time immemorial before that. Naturally, the gene might not carry forward, but it still makes any one person you pick out on the street a very likely carrier. </div> </div> </div>I had always been under the impression that was the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-15-2014, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T16:08:23-07:00","id":217628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=217618#post217618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had always been under the impression that was the <i>point.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, A certain Mongolian has his DNA pattern reflected in 1 in 200 men and that was only back to the roman era. Dial that back to the dawn of freakin' time, and you got Daddy Wolf's DNA pattern floating around in every single human on earth.<br /> <br /> Which again leads credence to the idea that all that is needed for a person to change is to have the insane moon god (or their followers) decide them to be.<br /> <br /> Of course, there is really nothing stopping said moon god(dess) from beating some poor guy who doesn't have daddy wolf's history with the Change, and saying &quot;you're in my army now&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T17:18:12-07:00","id":217679,"title":"","content":"@Satchel: Guess the quotation markers around the &quot;the werewolf gene&quot; didn't convey what I was getting at. I'll give you the long version, then. If breeding and legacy influence the chance of an Uratha Changing, then you've got potential data that says &quot;persons who are related to X werewolf have a higher-than-average possibility of being werewolves themselves.&quot; The wolf-blooded merit presently implies this much, that a lineage close to Uratha makes you more likely to become one. Hunter Team Alpha takes out a werewolf, takes a sample, and puts that into a bank of known werewolves. Hunter Agency checks that against genealogical records and test results from said bloodwork to find near relatives of that person, since, as you pointed out, many Uratha drop off the grid and may impregnate someone without leaving a record. Methodical Hunter Agency will flag these individuals and keep an eye out for them. Crazy Hunter Agency disappears the ones that are too-closely-related. Look up Operation Twelfth Night in War Against the Pure, and you've got hunters who are driven enough and have enough backing to try these kinds of shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Thus, I tend to run that lineage doesn't meaningfully-influence Changing.<br /> <br /> As for my second remark, that's, indeed, the point. My implication, then, becomes that the ability to trace your lineage to a point where it was touched by the spiritual influence that seems at present to be necessary for a werewolf is moot. Thus, the more meaningful mechanism becomes the Chosen aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T22:35:14-07:00","id":217892,"title":"","content":"Some of the early promo stuff for WtF was along those lines, when comparing to the &quot;born Garou&quot; from WtA games, to explain that any person in the world, at any point in their lives, could become Uratha because Luna chooses them and decides when they change, not genetics.<br /> <br /> But that's been years now, and I don't remember if it was forum posts, official releases, or what at this point. Or if my memory is making it all up because that's how I want it to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T16:01:50-07:00","id":218589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tilting Clock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=217679#post217679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Satchel: Guess the quotation markers around the &quot;the werewolf gene&quot; didn't convey what I was getting at. I'll give you the long version, then. If breeding and legacy influence the chance of an Uratha Changing, then you've got potential data that says &quot;persons who are related to X werewolf have a higher-than-average possibility of being werewolves themselves.&quot; The wolf-blooded merit presently implies this much, that a lineage close to Uratha makes you more likely to become one. Hunter Team Alpha takes out a werewolf, takes a sample, and puts that into a bank of known werewolves. Hunter Agency checks that against genealogical records and test results from said bloodwork to find near relatives of that person, since, as you pointed out, many Uratha drop off the grid and may impregnate someone without leaving a record. Methodical Hunter Agency will flag these individuals and keep an eye out for them. Crazy Hunter Agency disappears the ones that are too-closely-related. Look up Operation Twelfth Night in War Against the Pure, and you've got hunters who are driven enough and have enough backing to try these kinds of shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would work if said Hunter Agency had 1) Virtually infinite resources; 2) Incredibly crappy threat assessment and last but not least 3) the drive of freakin' terrorists.<br /> <br /> Not even the God Machine can pull something like that as effectively as you described it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T17:34:54-07:00","id":218629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=218589#post218589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would work if said Hunter Agency had 1) Virtually infinite resources; 2) Incredibly crappy threat assessment and last but not least 3) the drive of freakin' terrorists.<br /> <br /> Not even the God Machine can pull something like that as effectively as you described it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless ST fiat was implemented, but yeah, we'd also have to assume the Uratha would just &quot;let them&quot; kill all the wolf-blooded. Then again, Conspiracies like Charon or Task Force: Valkyrie could potentially do something like that to a certain degree as the focus of a Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T19:02:14-07:00","id":218675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tilting Clock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=217679#post217679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my second remark, that's, indeed, the point. My implication, then, becomes that the ability to trace your lineage to a point where it was touched by the spiritual influence that seems at present to be necessary for a werewolf is moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Hence my pointing out of <i>notable ancestors</i> as a greater focus of attempts to trace Uratha lineage - the strength of the wolf's blood in you appears to vary based on more than familial factors - there's a chicken-and-egg thing at work where &quot;wilder&quot; people seem to have a stronger spiritual footprint and a greater likelihood of giving birth to werewolves than more &quot;normal&quot; children-of-children of werewolves.<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;trace your lineage back to a Celestine in prehistory&quot; that's important. It's &quot;you are made from the stuff that produced this, that, and the other renowned skinchanging wolfperson of legend, and you bear some of the same traits that made the spirits view them as worthy of power.&quot; There is no singular &quot;the&quot; spiritual influence at play here to a meaningful degree.<br /> <br /> Most of those records are likely to be recorded in the First Tongue in Uratha oral tradition and are unlikely to mention the werewolves by anything but their deed name. Most of the people who become werewolves <i>become werewolves</i> and thus fall off the grid after the Change. Killing off wolf-blooded is going to accomplish precisely nothing useful thanks to the aforementioned nearly-everybody's-a-carrier thing; doubly so now that the Uratha can safely breed amongst themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thus, the more meaningful mechanism becomes the Chosen aspect. </div> </div> </div>In case it wasn't clear, I thoroughly disagree with the premise that the Uratha are &quot;bred rather than chosen&quot; in anything but the most meaninglessly broad sense of &quot;having this degree of lineage makes you more likely to be seen as worthy of the curse of lycanthropy, for all that 'more likely' means anything when Luna is involved.&quot; As has already been pointed out, strictly-breeding-based werewolfism is nearer to Apocalypse's bailiwick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T08:24:02-07:00","id":219103,"title":"","content":"Eh, it's pretty irrelevant since at the end of the day, Uratha are gonna be able to make people into wolfbloods in Idigam Chronicle. And I wouldn't rule out some rite that then turns them into Uratha afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T20:14:03-07:00","id":225605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163531-if-shapechangers-were-chosen-instead-of-bred?p=209940#post209940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cleave to the human won't matter after idigam anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is the first I've heard of the Oath of the Moon being changed. Where did you hear about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T21:44:51-07:00","id":225641,"title":"","content":"Lyrics' probably referring to the fact that they're getting rid of the unihar concept and allowing uratha to breed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wolf-blooded/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wolf-blooded/\" target=\"_blank\"> Wolf-Blooded &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wolf-blooded/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/wolf-blooded/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;And yes, werewolves can have children with other werewolves. Unihar have a bunch of unfortunate implications, so we\u2019ve quietly excised them. Something like the unihar may show up later, but it\u2019s not going to be in the same context at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's down in the comments section.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T22:00:46-07:00","id":225649,"title":"","content":"That's pretty neat. On the one hand, I was kinda looking forward to some potential story hooks that Unihar would have been involved with. On the other hand, new possibilities as well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}